  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Some prime numbers can be expressed as a sum of other consecutive prime numbers.\n\n**For Example**\n\n\n5=2+35 = 2 + 35=2+3,\n17=2+3+5+717 = 2 + 3 + 5 + 717=2+3+5+7,\n41=2+3+5+7+11+1341 = 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 + 1341=2+3+5+7+11+13.\nYour task is to find out how many prime numbers which satisfy this property are present in the range 333 to NNN subject to a constraint that summation should always start with number 222.\n\nWrite code to find out the number of prime numbers that satisfy the above-mentioned property in a given range.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer NNN\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint the total number of all such prime numbers which are less than or equal to NNN.",
    "constraints": [
      "2&lt;N≤1052 \\lt N \\leq 10^{5}2&lt;N≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
